Package: bubblequiz
Title: Print, Scan and Auto-Mark Multiple-Choice Bubble Sheets
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Will", "Cornwell", email = "wcornwell@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Will Cornwell [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Will Cornwell <wcornwell@gmail.com>
Description: An end-to-end toolkit for paper multiple-choice exams. Define the
    exam shape once in a YAML config, generate shuffled question-paper versions
    and a matching printable OMR answer sheet, then grade the scanned sheets
    with the Claude vision API and score them against the answer key. Designed
    to be installed once and called from any course repository.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    yaml,
    readr,
    dplyr,
    tibble,
    pdftools,
    magick,
    httr2,
    jsonlite,
    base64enc,
    curl,
    qpdf,
    stats,
    tools,
    utils
Suggests:
    optparse
SystemRequirements: pandoc, xelatex, poppler, ImageMagick
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
